jumped into section one, which was about data

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:46.320
management.

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:56.110
So data management, we heard about indexing
and binding data within the data management

00:00:56.110 --> 00:00:58.580
section.

00:00:58.580 --> 00:01:03.410
But mainly about how to make data that is
usable.

00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:08.510
So how to make data that's well curated, following
standards for metadata, and including prominent

00:01:08.510 --> 00:01:09.510
information.

00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:12.130
Now we're into section two.

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:18.080
Section two is titled Data Representation,
but really it's about getting data into usable

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:19.080
format.

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:22.150
This will take us through the end of the calendar
year.

00:01:22.150 --> 00:01:27.420
And then starting next year in 2017, we'll
start up again with a section on computing

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:32.210
followed by a section on analysis, and then
other topics like ethics.

00:01:32.210 --> 00:01:37.040
Can you go to the next slide?

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:39.100
So I'm sorry, I have a mistake here.

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:44.049
I should be highlighting the section two data
representation, which is where we're at, not

00:01:44.049 --> 00:01:45.049
computing.

00:01:45.049 --> 00:01:50.000
But data representation includes topics such
as databases and data warehouses, wrangling,

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.030
normalization of pre-processing.

00:01:52.030 --> 00:01:58.659
Those topics we have two guest speakers speak
on that for two weeks.

00:01:58.659 --> 00:02:01.110
And then natural language processing and exploratory
data analysis.

00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:06.350
But today we are incredibly lucky-- can you
go to the next slide?

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:15.950
We're incredibly lucky to have with us Dr.
Anita Bandrowski, who is currently at UCSD

00:02:15.950 --> 00:02:20.280
and has a background in both neurophysiology
and bioinformatics.

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:26.919
She trained in neurophysiology at UC Riverside
